<title>FRANCE: CADES says 1996 RDS revenue close to 21.5 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>CADES says 1996 RDS revenue close to 21.5 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French welfare debt repayment fund CADES said on Tuesday its 1996 revenue from the so-called RDS &quot;welfare tax&quot; would be very close to 21.5 billion francs ($3.7 billion).</p>
<p>Benoit Jolivet, president of the fund, told a news briefing the amount would be &quot;extremely close&quot; to that figure, which is line with initial CADES forecasts.</p>
<p>Official accounts will be published at the end of April or the beginninng of May, he said.  </p>
<p>Jolivet said receipts for 1997 should be between 25 and 25.5 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
